# Architecture

The map is [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md). Product rules stay in [docs/ai/domain-model.md](docs/ai/domain-model.md). Do not copy those rules here.

## Where code goes

- `src/app/`: routes, layouts, and route handlers. A page may read Prisma and pass plain data to components.
- `src/components/ui/`: shared primitives. No actions, Prisma, or `next-auth`.
- `src/components/layout/`: shell, header, navigation.
- `src/components/auth/`: session UI.
- `src/components/site/`: physician-site feature UI. It may import server actions and Zod. It must not import Prisma.
- `src/components/providers/`: app-wide providers.
- `src/lib/actions/`: server actions. `ActionState` lives in `state.ts`.
- `src/lib/validators/`: Zod schemas. No Prisma and no React.
- `src/lib/access.ts`: current user, physician, and patient.
- `src/lib/auth.ts`: NextAuth options. Server only.
- `src/lib/prisma.ts`: Prisma client and the physician insert guard. Server only.
- `src/lib/physician-site.ts`: the singleton public physician read.
- `src/lib/money.ts`: the price bound and bigint-to-number conversion.
- `src/lib/storage.ts` and `src/lib/uploads.ts`: local images. Server only.
- `prisma/`: schema, new migrations, and the local seed.

Use kebab-case file names. Do not add a barrel `index.ts` for every folder. Do not rename `components/site`.

## Components

A component owns one workflow. Extract a sibling when a second workflow appears, as `ServiceImageField` and `DeleteServiceButton` sit beside `ServiceForm`. Do not extract a component that is used once and has no separate responsibility. Do not split the primitives in `components/ui`.

Keep functions and React components as functions. Do not add classes, repositories, or a dependency-injection container.

## Imports

- Client components must not import `src/lib/prisma.ts`, `src/lib/auth.ts`, `src/lib/storage.ts`, or `src/lib/physician-site.ts`.
- Validators and `src/lib/money.ts` must not import Prisma or React.
- Actions may use access, validators, Prisma, and storage.
- While `cacheComponents` is enabled, a server read of cookies, headers, or the database calls `connection()` from `next/server`.

## Behavior

Business rules for requests, prices, and ownership live in server actions and Zod. Client checks are only immediate feedback.

Authorize with `currentPhysician` or `currentPatient`, then scope the query by that id. Do not trust a posted profile id.

Prices cross into client components as `number`, through `displayPrices`. The cap is `1000000000000`.

Public physician reads use `findPublicPhysician` (`singleton: 1`).

Unexpected database errors return a generic Persian message and log a static event name, not the request body.

Before a bugfix, name the caller, the input, and the observable result. Preserve that result unless a reviewed defect says it is wrong.

## Schema and tests

Schema changes are new migrations. Do not edit applied SQL. Do not drop `service_requests_one_pending`, `medical_services_price_bounds`, or `physician_profiles_singleton_is_one`.

Tests for pure rules live in `tests/` and run with `pnpm test`. Do not place a `*.test.ts` file beside application modules. That script does not migrate or seed.
